<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Viromandui</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Belgic people of the upper Somme whose name lives on in the Vermandois and the town of Vermand.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Viromandui lived in the upper valleys of the Somme and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oise">Oise</a>, between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nervii">Nervii</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ambiani">Ambiani</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/suessiones">Suessiones</a>. Caesar records that they promised ten thousand warriors to the Belgic league of 57 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers or institutions. Excavations at Vermand have revealed a large fortified site of the period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They fought beside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nervii">Nervii</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/atrebates">Atrebates</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-sabis">Battle of the Sabis</a> in 57 BCE and were defeated. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-quentin">Augusta Viromanduorum</a> (Saint-Quentin), and the medieval <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-vermandois">County of Vermandois</a> kept their name.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/viromandui.jpg" alt="Viromandui" width="320" height="422"><figcaption>Image: pour le versement et le modifications : G.Garitan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camp_de_Vermand_35044.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=viromandui" aria-label="Viromandui on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4761 453 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Viromandui lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5081 709L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5081 709h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5081 709h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=viromandui">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

